# BUG-572: an `extend` body is checked by the front end. `toUpper` is not a str method (it is
# `upper`), and before the fix `zebra -c` passed this -- the checker had no arm for `extend`
# -- so zig reported it later with no column. QUICKSTART §42's own example had this line.
extend str
    def shout(): str
        return this.toUpper() + "!"

def main()
    print("hello".shout())
